    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d441">

                <pb facs="0542" n="534" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg534"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 (D) Regulations/4797: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-30T18:00:00-05:00">September 30, 1941—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>515. Reference Department’s 352, September 22.<anchor n="61" xml:id="d441-f1"/> I
                    am pleased to report that Metals Reserve representative Smith this afternoon <pb
                        facs="0543" n="535" xml:id="pg535"/> signed the agreement with the Director
                    General of Finance. Official communiqué will be published Thursday
                        morning<anchor n="62" xml:id="d441-f2"/> containing résumé of agreement with
                    short explanation of how basic prices are determined and description of “floor
                    under market principle”. It is requested that you withhold publicity until
                    Thursday morning, that is until after the Government communiqué has been
                    published here.</p>
                <p>According to a statement of the Finance Minister the Government of Peru has
                    decided to terminate molybdenum shipments to Japan as of today. British
                    diplomatic authorities in Lima informed me today that Great Britain will
                    definitely purchase the residue of the 1941 molybdenum contract with Japan as
                    well as the 83 metric tons salvaged from the German vessel <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Monserrate.</hi></p>
                <p>Chargeable to Metals Reserve Company.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
